1001 TV — Technical User Feedback
Account & Authentication
●	Sign-in is limited to phone number + OTP, with no email or third-party (Google/Apple) authentication option.
●	OTP delivery is inconsistent; there were cases where the code arrived late or the retry/resend flow did not reset the timer correctly.
●	Error messages during failed login are generic and don't specify whether the issue is network, invalid code, or server-side.
Video Playback
●	Occasional buffering/freezing during playback, suggesting adaptive bitrate switching isn't always smooth on unstable connections.
●	No manual video quality selector, playback quality seems fully automatic with no user override.
●	Subtitle rendering has positioning issues on some titles, subtitles overlap on-screen text or sit too close to the edge.
●	Aspect ratio handling is inconsistent, black bars appear on some content even on devices that should support full-screen scaling.
●	No picture-in-picture support, and no 10-second skip forward/back controls.
Casting & Cross-Device
●	Casting from mobile to TV (Chromecast/similar) is not reliable, connection drops or fails to initiate on first attempt.
●	Continue Watching progress doesn't always sync in real time between mobile and TV sessions.
Smart TV / Android TV App
●	D-pad/remote navigation between rows and tiles is not always predictable, focus sometimes jumps or gets lost.
●	No QR-code login option for TV, login has to be done manually with the remote, which is slow.
●	Player controls on TV are less complete than on mobile (missing quality/subtitle settings).
Search & Discovery
●	No autocomplete or search-as-you-type suggestions.
●	Search doesn't appear to be typo-tolerant or handle Arabic/English title variants well.
●	No filtering by actor, director, or genre.
●	Home screen recommendations don't seem to reflect watch history, no "Because You Watched" or similar personalized rows.
Content & Positioning (positive)
●	Strong Iraqi and regional content library, combined with international titles.
●	1001 Originals add exclusive content not available on other apps I've used.
●	Sports integration in the same app is a good engagement driver.
●	Free tier alongside premium content lowers the barrier to try the service.
Summary
Content and positioning are strong. The main gaps I noticed as a user are in core app reliability: authentication flow, playback stability, TV navigation, and search/discovery. These are the areas that most directly affect day-to-day usability.

